ssive development. The most forcing and active move is **B: c1-g5**, which develops my last minor piece with purpose, controls important squares, and creates potential threats against Black's undeveloped position.\n\nReason: B: c1-g5 is the most active developing move available. It places the bishop on an excellent square where it controls key dark squares and prepares to create threats. Given my significant material disadvantage, I need to maximize piece activity and create complications rather than play passively. This move gets my last minor piece into the game with tempo and purpose.\n\nAnswer: B: c1-g5"}
